# Line endings, settled once.
#
# Without this, a Windows checkout with core.autocrlf=true writes CRLF into the
# working copy while the repo stores LF, so every line of every text file reads
# as modified with byte-identical content — twenty phantom diffs hiding the one
# real edit. `text=auto` still lets git detect binaries and leave them alone
# (logos/BridgeSuite.png stays untouched); `eol=lf` pins the working copy to what the
# repo already holds, on every platform.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Belt and braces for the one binary in the tree, so no future detection change
# can rewrite it.
*.png binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
